he mandates shutting down  the strip the effects on small business  and then subsequently the money that is  poured in and has been allocated by the  county and elsewhere  has the money gone to the right place  to help these small businesses yeah  absolutely I think that that it's proven  that for the small business owners  certainly in my district and across the  county this has kept them kept them able  to to have their doors open or to reopen  their doors after the pandemic and so I  think definitely the money went to the  right place and is continuing to to help  them we've got our small business grant  program that's going to get back up and  running now for those that want to  expand their operations we know  everyone's struggling to hire right now  and so we want to make sure that there  are opportunities for these small  business owners to create new jobs for  for people here in southern Nevada your  opponent also suggests that broadly in  Clark County there's a lot of money  being wasted there isn't enough of  watching of the money being spent  keeping an eye on where the taxpayers  money is going are you confident that  the contracts that are signed this is  kind of a broad question I realized but  do you think that the taxpayers are  being well served by you and the other  commissioner owners with their money I  think absolutely our CFO is one of the  frankly most conservative CFOs out there  pre-pandemic we were in the strongest  financial situation of any local  jurisdiction and we continue to be so  there's a reason why our bond ratings  are at the top of every jurisdiction in  the state of Nevada we are fiscally  conservative we make sure that we spend  every dollar in the right way and if any  issues come up we go audit those those  expenditures and we've clawed back money  when we found that there were issues out  there even from nonprofits one of uh an  issue that you have close to your heart  is the issue of Red Rock and protection  of Red Rock both uh as County  Commissioner and beforehand as well talk  about some of the efforts that you have  taken to try and protect Red Rock but  also increase access to it sure  absolutely um as as a lot of the viewers  might know there's been a big battle  between a developer and Clark County  over the last 20 years the original  proposal from the developer was for more  than 5 000 homes and the the County  Commission uh in 2019 had denied the  request from the developer to waive a  condition that related to the road the  developer finally after 20 years came in  with a proposal that was within the  density that was permitted up there when  he bought it and so that was the subject  of a recent vote on the County  Commission well it's also the subject of  litigation that you're involved in as  well your opponent is accusing you of  being corrupt there's allegations of  conflict of interest that you voted on  this even though before you were on the  commission your previous as an attorney  you were involved in this case  allegations of Records being deleted  public records being deleted how do you  respond to these accusations well sure I  think I've responded publicly to these  accusations before with regards to to  the vote and the allegations that I was  conflicted out that's why I firmatively  went to the Nevada Commission on ethics  laid everything out to them before that  a vote and they said that I was required  to disclose my prior affiliation with uh  with a non-profit say Red Rock but but  that I was not only allowed to vote but  that was my obligation on behalf of the  voters who elected me to participate in  those kinds of discussions is every  public record that comes came from your  office regarding this development with  the Mr Rhodes in that development is  every public record still accounted for  as far as I know okay  um let's move on to another aspect of  sort of broadly Clark County we were  talking before about business recovery  um what can be done in the next four  years if you're re-elected to try and  help get businesses back on their feet  because a lot of them are still  struggling and if you look at sort of  the the recovery of the economy in  southern Nevada there's no doubt there  is a recovery but it might be behind the  curve of a lot of other parts in the  country sure so I I sit on the Economic  Development Authority and uh as part of  the lvga we are really focusing on not  only bringing in new jobs into our  community here we've talked about  economic diversification in Nevada for  for decades now we don't ever seem to do  it when times are good we think great  the the strip is going to pay for  everything and I think for the first  time we're really focusing on not just  jobs but on jobs that matter in  manufacturing and technology and so we  are fostering those opportunities with  our with our director of community and  economic development at the county  something that we didn't have before and  that I'm very proud of having worked on  at the Clark County and as part of that  we're supporting those small business  owners we're expanding our Redevelopment  agency we're investing back into those  parts of the community that have really  faced challenges over the years and we  want to make sure that we Foster areas  like mine out in the out in the  southwest part of town where you'll see  our state bird the crane all over on on  the curve out there but we want to make  sure in in the older parts of town that  we're really investing in those areas  too so if you are re-elected  first County Commission meeting first a  day on the job in January 2023 what's  the first thing you really want to try  and Tackle well I think economic  development is is definitely top my  priority list affordable housing I think  we've already taken the the first  important steps in in funding a lot of  those priorities so I'll be focusing on  broadening our economic base bringing  new jobs to Nevada so that we can  continue the economic uptight here all  right commissioner Justin Jones running  for re-election in District F appreciate  the time sir thank you very much and  good luck thanks John

